<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12457"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 11:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point Steve, they say that the reason most Killers are not caught is because their intelligence is below our level, so therefore we can not think like they do, wemake things harder tan they really are. I am a Psy Nursing student and in the DMS-IV that we use for diagnostic and statistical determination of mental disorders  there are only four what are known as Axis&#39; in classification of disorders, the ones mentioned here all fall under Axis II Personality Disorders. that includes Narcissistic, Antisocial, socio, Psyco, an all others not specified fall into this asessment. I believe many just pick a generic term and use it, but that is ok too since we are all learning Thanks E. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
